{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"artifacthub/kyverno-policies/add-karpenter-daemonset-priority-class","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:18:28.655Z","source":{"name":"Artifact Hub","api":"https://artifacthub.io/api/v1/packages/kyverno/kyverno-policies/add-karpenter-daemonset-priority-class","page":"https://artifacthub.io/packages/kyverno/kyverno-policies/add-karpenter-daemonset-priority-class"},"readme":"When a DaemonSet is added to a cluster every node will get a new pod. There may not be \nenough room for this on every node. Karpenter cannot provision extra nodes just for the \nDaemonSet because the new pods are not scheduled the way regular pods are. It would require\nparallel scheduling logic that is not proper to Kubernetes. Therefore, eviction of regular \npods should happen instead. This can be achieved with the priority class system-node-critical.\n\nRefer to the documentation for more details on Kyverno annotations: https://artifacthub.io/docs/topics/annotations/kyverno/","readmeBase":"https://github.com/kyverno/policies","publisher":{"name":"Kyverno","url":"https://artifacthub.io/packages/search?org=kyverno","official":false,"verified":true,"cncf":true},"registered":null,"updated":"2023-06-01T16:55:10.000Z","categories":[],"keywords":["kyverno","Karpenter"],"license":null,"links":[{"name":"Kyverno Policies repository","url":"https://github.com/kyverno/policies"}],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":null,"stars":0,"subscriptions":0},"mediaTypes":[],"contentTypes":[],"storage":null,"tags":[{"name":"1.0.0","digest":"sha256:c2eb8e9fbe5cb962c927d67b38c3d47064431f0657a5ceb20286c1f73dcedf3a","pushed":"2023-06-01T16:55:10.000Z","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":null,"status":null,"appVersion":null}],"tagsTotal":1,"security":null,"install":"```shell\nkubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kyverno/policies/main/karpenter-mpol/add-karpenter-daemonset-priority-class/add-karpenter-daemonset-priority-class.yaml\n```","version":"1.0.0","appVersion":nu